  "worked_solution": "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y)\u2248f(a,b)+\u2207f(a,b)\\cdot \u27e8x-a,y-b\u27e9.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(1,-1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & \u2248f(1,-1)+\u2207f(1,-1)\\cdot \u27e8x-1,y-(-1)\u27e9 \\\\  & =f(1,-1)+\u27e8{f}_{x}(1,-1),{f}_{y}(1,-1)\u27e9\\cdot \u27e8x-1,y+1\u27e9 \\\\  & =-3+\u27e8-6,3\u27e9\\cdot \u27e8x-1,y+1\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can approximate $f(1.01,-0.99)$ by evaluating the linear approximation at $x=1.01$ and $y=-0.99,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1.01,-0.99) & \u2248-3+\u27e8-6,3\u27e9\\cdot \u27e81.01-1,-0.99+1\u27e9 \\\\  & =-3+\u27e8-6,3\u27e9\\cdot \u27e80.01,0.01\u27e9 \\\\  & =-3-6(0.01)+3(0.01) \\\\  & =-3-0.06+0.03 \\\\  & =-3.03\\end{aligned}\n$$",
